      "realname": "Aaliyah Dana Haughton",
      "profile": "American Singer, Actress, dancer, and Model. \n\nBorn January 16, 1979, in Brooklyn, New York City, USA.\n\nAaliyah released 3 albums within her lifetime: \"Age Ain't Nothing But A Number\", \"One In A Million\" and her praised self-titled album, \"Aaliyah\".\n\nAaliyah starred in 2 movies, \"Romeo Must Die\" and posthumously, \"Queen of the Damned\".\n\nDaughter of [a1772573], sister of [a666565]. Niece of Record Executive [a348491] and (by marriage) Soul legend [a135244]. Cousin of record executive [a171166] and rapper [a803218].\nMarried to controversial R&B Singer/Producer [a14646] from 1994-1995 (annulled). At the time of passing, in a relationship with (and had reportedly planned to marry) Hip-hop mogul [a174951].\n\nUpon releasing her debut album \"[m=100995]\" in 1994, Aaliyah gained a steadily growing reputation for helping to redefine contemporary R&B, pop and hip hop, earning her the nicknames the \"Princess of R&B\" and \"Queen of Urban pop\".\nA sophomore album \"[m=101004]\" was released in 1996, and her final album, \"[m=35220]\", appeared earlier in the year of her tragic death.\n\nAaliyah unfortunately died on August 25, 2001, in Marsh Harbour, Abaco Islands, The Bahamas (Aged 22) in an Airplane crash that also claimed the lives of 8 others after filming the music video for her single \"Rock The Boat\", featured on her third album, \"Aaliyah\".\n\nAaliyah's posthumous works range from 1 Movie and 2 singles: \"Poison featuring The Weeknd\" released in 2021 and \"Gone featuring Tank\" released in 2025.\n\nAaliyah has sold an estimated 24 to 32 million albums worldwide, alongside over 8 million certified sales in the United States.",
